engine/godot/issues/comments/3140041105","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109161#issuecomment-3140041105","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109161","id":3140041105,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67KTmR","user":{"login":"Lippanon","id":115422160,"node_id":"U_kgDOBuEz0A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/115422160?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon","html_url":"https://github.com/Lippanon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-31T13:45:48Z","updated_at":"2025-07-31T13:45:48Z","body":"Reproducible in: v4.5.beta.custom_build [71a994815]\nAs commented in the MRP, it works with SomeClass.new({}), so it doesn't make sense to me that it wouldn't work with load(path), sometimes one wants to create a script dynamically and can't use the class_name directly.\n\nAnd indeed, you can use foo({}) without error, for example in:\n```\nfunc foo(a_typed_dict: Dictionary[int, int]) -> void:\n\tprint(a_typed_dict)\n\tprint(\"is_typed: \", a_typed_dict.is_typed())\n```\n\nSomething similar happens with ternary operator (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/83026).","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3140041105/reactions","total_co