following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-31T14:59:58Z","updated_at":"2025-07-31T14:59:58Z","body":"The same problem (or inconsistency) occurs with call_group, for example:\n```\na_node.foo({}) # Works\nget_tree().call_group(\"test_group\", \"foo\", {}) # Fails with error\n```\n\nI suppose if there was a quick way to create an empty typed-array/dictionary, a consistent stricter type checking would be fine, but at the moment I think the only workaround is to create a typed variable before passing.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3140312682/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3140343249","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109161#issuecomment-3140343249","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109161","id":3140343249,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67LdXR","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-31T15:08:39Z","updated_at":"2025-07-31T15:08:39Z","body":"For the issue of creating empty cases that's tracked in the discussion I linked above, but a simple around should be: `Dictionary({}, TYPE_INT, &\"\", null, TYPE_INT, &\"\", null)`","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3140343249/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3140660642","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109161#issuecomment-3140660642","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109161","id":3140660642,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67Mq2i","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-31T16:47:48Z","updated_at":"2025-07-31T16:52:40Z","body":"In an untyped context, array and dictionary literals (`[]` and `{}` syntax) create untyped arrays and dictionaries. You can use temporary local variables or type casting with the `as` operator (only works with literals) to create a typed array/dictionary. For example, `[1, 2, 3] as Array[int]` instead of `[1, 2, 3]`. In the future, we would like to add a typed constructor, like `Array[int]([1, 2, 3])`.\n\n* See also https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/71336 and other issues that mention this PR.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3140660642/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3140694243","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109161#issuecomment-3140694243","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109161","id":3140694243,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67MzDj","user":{"login":"Lippanon","id":115422160,"node_id":"U_kgDOBuEz0A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/115422160?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon","html_url":"https://github.com/Lippanon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-31T16:58:00Z","updated_at":"2025-07-31T16:58:00Z","body":"I understand but isn't calling `a_node.foo({})` creating an untyped dictionary? And foo expects typed but it doesn't complain or give an error, it gets inferred to typed. So why doesn't `_init` do that when using `load`? Or `call_group`? You don't consider that inconsistency a bug (since you're removing the bug label)?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3140694243/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3140814967","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109161#issuecomment-3140814967","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109161","id":3140814967,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67NQh3","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-31T17:34:28Z","updated_at":"2025-07-31T17:34:28Z","body":"> var _new_ref: SomeClass = load(\"res://some_class.gd\").new({}) # Fails\n\n`load()` returns a value of the static type `Resource`, not a concrete GDScript class (unlike if you used `preload()`). Therefore, the `new()` call is unknown to the GDScript static analyzer. It does not know what arguments the constructor takes, and therefore does not convert passed array/dictionary literals to typed ones.\n\nHaving the influence of (un)typed context in a dynamic language is confusing for users, but we have what we have. Personally, I would prefer `[]` and `{}` to **always** create untyped arrays/dictionaries, and have a separate syntax for typed ones (`Array[T]([])` and `Dictionary[TKey, TValue]({})`). But this is not possible for compatibility reasons.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3140814967/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]